    37	    """
    38	    Drop the singleton marker into the matching red U-shaped container, or make a bottom-row puddle if no closed container is hit.
    39	
    40	    Input structure
    41	    - The grid has a dominant background, one singleton marker pixel on the top row,
    42	      and one other foreground color forming vertical bars and bottom segments.
    43	    - A closed container is a U shape: two vertical side bars with a continuous
    44	      bottom segment between them and an empty rectangular interior above the bottom.
    45	
    46	    Rule
    47	    - Remove the top marker from its original cell.
    48	    - If exactly one closed U-shaped container has the marker column within its
    49	      horizontal footprint, fill that container's empty interior with the marker color.
    50	    - If no closed container is under the marker column, fill the whole bottom row
    51	      with the marker color.
    52	
    53	    Key insight
    54	    - The marker does not identify a color by value; it identifies a vertical drop
    55	      column, and only a structurally closed U shape can catch and contain the fill.
    56	    """
